# godocs profile — hole-godocs
# https://github.com/the-hole-foundation/hole-godocs
#
# Activated by adding "godocs" to `projects` in ~/.config/chezmoi/chezmoi.toml.
# See docs/profiles/godocs.md for what this installs and what is manual.
#
# Anything that already lives in dot_Brewfile.core is intentionally NOT
# duplicated here. As of 2026-06-02 core already provides:
#   git, gh, lazygit, jq, fd, ripgrep, doppler, uv, pyenv
# Core also ships an unversioned `go` (Homebrew latest). This profile pins a
# parallel `go@1.25` to match the upstream `go.mod` toolchain directive —
# both can coexist (go@1.25 is keg-only, accessed by full path or PATH munge).
#
# LibreOffice is intentionally NOT listed here. On Linuxbrew it isn't a
# formula and Homebrew Cask is macOS-only, so the run_once script handles
# both platforms (apt on Linux, cask on macOS). Keeping it out of the
# Brewfile means `brew bundle list --file=dot_Brewfile.godocs` works on
# any platform.

# ── Go toolchain pinned to upstream go.mod ──────────────────────────────────
# Keg-only; the run_once script wires it onto PATH for the project.
brew "go@1.25"

# ── R2 / S3-compatible storage ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# rclone: primary tool for syncing hole-godocs corpora to/from Cloudflare R2.
# awscli: AWS SDK v2 used by the Go code targets R2 over the S3 API; the CLI
#   is the operator-side debugging companion (signed URL generation, head-
#   object checks, presign rotation).
brew "rclone"
brew "awscli"

# ── PDF rendering / extraction ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# mupdf + mupdf-tools: `mutool` + `mupdf-x11` viewer used by
# test-mupdf.sh in the godocs repo for layout-aware page extraction.
# Board decision Q2 = YES — the container must be self-sufficient for
# document rendering, so we ship this in the profile rather than relying
# on the developer's workstation.
brew "mupdf"
brew "mupdf-tools"
